    "body": "<!-- cubic:v=4123241d-77e3-4f42-af5e-4fefe57b707b -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP1: `__starship_update_columns` clobbers `$?` before it is captured for `--status`/`--pipestatus`, causing the prompt to always report exit status 0\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At src/init/starship.zsh, line 51:\n\n<comment>`__starship_update_columns` clobbers `$?` before it is captured for `--status`/`--pipestatus`, causing the prompt to always report exit status 0</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -29,6 +48,8 @@ fi\n \n # Runs before each new command line.\n prompt_starship_precmd() {\n+    __starship_update_columns\n+\n     # Save the status, because subsequent commands in this function will change $?\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>",
